# Confluence update

## Gate

Update **only** when the user names an existing page (id, or title + space)
or explicitly says to revise / refresh / fix a known Confluence page.

Do not invent a page id. Resolve via `confluence_get_page` or
`confluence_search` first.

## Prefer section updates

1. Read the current page (`confluence_get_page`) so headings and macros are
   known.
2. Prefer `confluence_update_page_section` for a single H2 change — leaves
   other sections, macros, and layouts alone.
3. Use full `confluence_update_page` only when the user asked for a rewrite
   or the change spans most sections.
4. Never delete or rewrite storage-format macros you do not understand
   (draw.io macros, Jira issue macros, includes, layouts).

## Body discipline

- Keep stable H2 names when possible so future section updates stay cheap.
- New durable topics → add a new H2 rather than bloating Overview.
- Follow `atlassian-confluence-structure` for any new sections you introduce.
- Comments: prefer `confluence_add_comment` / inline comment tools for review
  notes; do not bury review chatter in page body unless asked.

## Diagrams

Replacing or adding a figure: `atlassian-confluence-diagrams`. Prefer uploading a new
attachment version over rewriting unrelated page XML.

## Done

Return what changed (section names or “full rewrite”), page id, and browse
URL when known. Stop — do not implement product code unless the user added
an explicit implement verb.
